# examples/ ships source only — every compiled-backend artifact (.py, .c, .cpp,
# native binaries with no extension, etc.) is a local build byproduct, not
# something to track. Allowlist instead of chasing extensions: a bare `*` deny
# plus explicit `!` exceptions catches every backend's output naming
# convention at once, including a same-stem extensionless binary (the C/CPP/RS
# backends' own default `-o` behavior, `base` with no extension, right next to
# the source) that no extension-based pattern would ever cover.
*
!*.ac
!.gitignore
